& [SJS]
  + Situation: Slice4A closes exact proof-carrying paths and channel accounts while lexical association still exists only as an unindexed legacy substring scan
  + Justification: a deterministic source-resolving token sidecar is the minimum structure needed for fast lexical association but coupling query changes to index formation would risk exact wire compatibility and enlarge the first proof surface
  + Solution: activate only strict sidecar forms tokenizer compiler canonical replay and adversarial tests in Slice4B1 then require separate Slice4B2 authority for query budget match-account and scanner behavior

& [CompletedWorkReview]
  + Slice2 already supplies validated catalogue roots exact addresses labels meaning references packages source anchors and admitted-fabric replay
  + Slice3 exact scanner remains a complete independent consumer and supplies no authority to lexical code
  + Slice4A completion proof supplies the typed evidence and canonical recomputation pattern and satisfies the readiness dependency
  + the P1 verifier closes the workspace verification lane but grants no product semantics

& [ConflictResolved]
  + readiness recommended maximum_lexical_postings inside AnchorBudget while also requiring AnchorQuery and exact result bytes to remain stable
  + adding a required field to the current closed AnchorBudget would change the exact query wire form and every initializer even before lexical behavior is requested
  + Slice4B1 therefore makes no AnchorBudget or query-form change
  + Slice4B2 must choose a distinct lexical query wrapper or LexicalAnchorBudget under preserved source before any lexical discovery

& [FormDecision]
  + sidecar identity is independent from DerivedSemanticAnchorCatalogue and binds both catalogue_root and fabric_root
  + tokenizer identity binds profile compiler id compiler version and fixture digest
  + LexicalSurfaceKind is closed to preferred expression alias and meaning
  + each posting binds normalized token exact address surface kind surface digest positive occurrence count and exact evidence references
  + postings are canonically grouped by token without copying raw surface prose
  + occurrence count is observation only and cannot become relevance authority in this slice

& [TokenizerDecision]
  + accept the readiness Unicode-lowercase alphanumeric-run profile as cantor-lexical-tokenizer/0.1
  + bind the Rust compiler and adversarial fixture digest because standard-library Unicode behavior is compiled behavior
  + composed and decomposed forms intentionally remain distinct unless their declared lowercase and alphanumeric token sequences happen to coincide
  + no normalization confusable fuzzy synonym stemming stop-word n-gram or learned behavior is admitted

& [DerivationDecision]
  + validate and canonical-rebuild the exact catalogue against the same admitted SemanticFabric before indexing
  + preferred and alias bytes come from IdentityAnchorEntry while meaning bytes exact-resolve through meaning_ref to the admitted SemanticUnit
  + derive domain-separated surface index and proof digests
  + whole-index validation fresh-derives from exact request catalogue and fabric then compares complete equality
  + all work is pure in-memory deterministic Rust over caller-supplied admitted objects

& [BoundsDecision]
  + bind finite constants for surface token collection posting evidence revision and serialized index dimensions before implementation
  + refuse an over-bound derivation without returning a partial sidecar
  + do not add a query-time posting-union budget until Slice4B2 because no query occurs in Slice4B1

& [TestDecision]
  + strict serde unknown-field and unsupported-profile cases
  + ASCII mixed-case punctuation numeric one-character non-Latin combining and composed-decomposed tokenizer fixtures
  + preferred alias meaning empty repeated token repeated surface and canonical ordering cases
  + stale root wrong meaning correspondence profile compiler fixture surface digest token occurrence evidence omission addition reorder index-root and proof-digest mutations
  + equal derivation and serialized-byte equality plus whole-index canonical replay
  + existing exact catalogue and scanner focused and workspace regression remain mandatory

& [SevenFoldTrace]
  + fold_1 preserves the activation source Slice4A completion exact module identities and readiness rationale
  + fold_2 separates source fabric exact catalogue lexical sidecar query operator and future learned router identities
  + fold_3 defines tokenizer surface posting index request fault bound and digest forms
  + fold_4 traces every posting to exact surface address meaning unit package source catalogue and fabric roots
  + fold_5 excludes all query rank gate candidate cursor result provider learned persistence remote and effect behavior
  + fold_6 phase-locks tokenizer mutation replay bound and exact-regression fixtures before code
  + fold_7 converges on a small independently testable compiler waist for later lexical query consumption

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty labels token membership and occurrence as lexical evidence only and keeps unsupported semantics absent
  + Security requires admitted roots exact correspondence finite bounds closed profiles canonical replay and no self-authorizing sidecar
  + Weaver constructs addressable token-to-surface-to-identity associations without ranking or selection authority
  + Planner places catalogue validation source resolution tokenization canonical projection and digest closure in dependency order
  + Refiner isolates the smallest reusable sidecar compiler and defers the conflicting query-shape decision
  + Scribe retains exact surface digests evidence identities occurrence accounts roots and failure stages
  + Observer requires focused mutation proof plus unchanged exact scanner workspace lint format evidence and diff gates

